INSERT INTO skills_fts (id, name, owner, repo, category, search_text) VALUES ('Edgame2/castiel2/create-event-handlers', 'create-event-handlers', 'Edgame2', 'castiel2', 'community', 'create-event-handlers Edgame2 castiel2 community The create-event-handlers skill sets up RabbitMQ event publishers and consumers, following the ModuleImplementationGuide.md Section 9. It benefits developers working with tenant-only context and event-driven architectures. 创建事件处理程序以设置RabbitMQ事件发布者和消费者，遵循ModuleImplementationGuide.md第9节 イベントハンドラーを作成してRabbitMQイベントパブリッシャーとコンシューマーを設定します。ModuleImplementationGuide.mdの第9節に従います 이벤트 핸들러를 생성하여 RabbitMQ 이벤트 발행자 및 소비자를 설정합니다. ModuleImplementationGuide.md의 9절을 따릅니다 El skill ''create-event-handlers'' configura editores y consumidores de eventos de RabbitMQ. Sigue la guía de implementación de módulos para crear eventos con nombre de dominio, entidad y acción Le skill ''create-event-handlers'' configure les éditeurs et les consommateurs d''événements de RabbitMQ. Suivez le guide d''implémentation de modules pour créer des événements avec un nom de domaine, d''entité et d''action Das Skill ''create-event-handlers'' konfiguriert RabbitMQ-Ereignisveröffentlicher und -verbraucher. Befolgen Sie den Leitfaden für die Modulimplementierung, um Ereignisse mit Domänen-, Entitäts- und Aktionennamen zu erstellen Criar tratadores de eventos com RabbitMQ para publicação e consumo de eventos Настройка обработчиков событий с RabbitMQ для публикации и потребления событий إنشاء معالجات الأحداث باستخدام RabbitMQ لنشر واستهلاك الأحداث how to use create-event-handlers create-event-handlers setup guide RabbitMQ event publishers tenant-only context event naming convention create-event-handlers vs RabbitMQ create-event-handlers install what is create-event-handlers create-event-handlers alternative event-driven architecture with create-event-handlers AIエージェント 创建事件处理程序 RabbitMQ事件发布者 RabbitMQ事件消费者 事件命名约定 tenantId ModuleImplementationGuide.md 事件处理程序设置 AI工具 Sets up RabbitMQ event publishers and consumers following ModuleImplementationGuide.md Section 9 Follows a specific event naming convention: {domain}.{entity}.{action} Supports tenant-only context using tenantId Excludes organizationId from event payloads and createBaseEvent Adheres to guidelines outlined in ModuleImplementationGuide.md Section 9.1 Generates events in the format of user.created, auth.login.success, and notification.email.sent create-event-handlers is a skill that sets up RabbitMQ event publishers and consumers, following a specific event naming convention and tenant-only context.');
