PostgreSQL: Mejores Prácticas para Desar...","fr":"Conception de Tables PostgreSQL : Guide de Configuration","de":"PostgreSQL-Tabellendesign: Setup-Anleitung für Entwickler","pt":"Guia de Configuração para PostgreSQL Table Design","ru":"Настройка таблицы PostgreSQL: лучшие практики","ar":"إعداد جدول PostgreSQL: دليل إعداد معايير الأمان"},"description":{"en":"Learn how to optimize your PostgreSQL table design with expert tips and tricks. Discover the importance of primary keys, normalization, and denormalization f...","zh":"了解 PostgreSQL 表设计的核心规则和最佳实践，包括定义主键、 Normalize 和 Denormalize","ja":"PostgreSQL テーブル設計のベストプラクティスを学びましょう - PRIMARY KEY の定義、 Normalize、Denormalize など","ko":"PostgreSQL 테이블 설계를 위한 핵심 규칙과 최적화 전략 - PRIMARY KEY, Normalize, Denormalize 등","es":"Aprende a diseñar tablas en PostgreSQL de manera efectiva con nuestras mejores prácticas y recomendaciones para desarrolladores","fr":"Découvrez les meilleures pratiques pour concevoir des tables PostgreSQL avec notre guide de configuration pour les développeurs","de":"Erfahren Sie, wie Sie Tabellen in PostgreSQL effektiv entwerfen, mit unseren Best Practices und Empfehlungen für Entwickler","pt":"Aprenda a projetar tabelas no PostgreSQL com eficiência, seguindo as regras de normalização e denormalização para melhorar o desempenho","ru":"Узнайте, как проектировать таблицы в PostgreSQL эффективно, соблюдая правила нормализации и денормализации для повышения производительности","ar":"تعرف على كيفية تصميم الجداول في PostgreSQL بفعالية، باتباع قواعد التطبيع والتنظيم لإحسان الأداء"},"definition":{"en":"postgresql-table-design is a set of guidelines and best practices for creating efficient and scalable database tables in PostgreSQL, focusing on primary keys, normalization, and denormalization.","zh":"PostgreSQL 表设计是指为 PostgreSQL 数据库设计和优化表结构的过程","ja":"PostgreSQL テーブル設計とは、PostgreSQL データベースのテーブル構造を設計および最適化するプロセスです","ko":"PostgreSQL 테이블 설계는 PostgreSQL 데이터베이스의 테이블 구조를 설계하고 최적화하는 과정입니다","es":"El diseño de tablas PostgreSQL se refiere a la creación de estructuras de datos eficientes para almacenar y recuperar información","fr":"La conception de tables PostgreSQL fait référence à la création de structures de données efficaces pour stocker et récupérer des informations","de":"Das Tabellendesign in PostgreSQL bezieht sich auf die Erstellung effizienter Datenstrukturen zum Speichern und Abrufen von Informationen","pt":"O design de tabelas PostgreSQL é o processo de criar estruturas de dados eficientes para armazenar e gerenciar informações","ru":"Проектирование таблиц PostgreSQL - это процесс создания эффективных структур данных для хранения и управления информацией","ar":"تصميم الجداول في PostgreSQL هو عملية إنشاء هياكل البيانات الفعالة لتخزين وإدارة المعلومات"},"features":{"en":["Defines primary keys using BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","Normalizes data to 3NF to eliminate redundancy and update anomalies","Denormalizes data for high-ROI reads with proven join performance issues","Uses UUID for global uniqueness and opacity when necessary","Optimizes table design for time-series, event, and log data"],"zh":["定义主键（PRIMARY KEY）"," Normalize 到 3NF","仅在必要时 Denormalize","使用 BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","使用 UUID 时考虑全局唯一性和不透明性"],"ja":["PRIMARY KEY の定義"," Normalize を 3NF にする","必要な場合のみ Denormalize を実行","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY を使用","UUID を使用する場合はグローバル一意性と不透明性を考慮"],"ko":["PRIMARY KEY 정의","Normalize를 3NF로 수행","필요한 경우에만 Denormalize를 실행","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY 사용","UUID를 사용할 때는 글로벌 유일성과 불투명성을 고려"],"es":["Definir claves primarias con BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","Normalizar tablas hasta 3NF para eliminar redundancias de datos","Denormalizar tablas solo para lecturas de alto rendimiento","Usar UUID solo cuando se requiere unicidad global","Evitar la denormalización prematura para mantener la integridad de los datos"],"fr":["Définir des clés primaires avec BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","Normaliser les tables jusqu''à 3NF pour éliminer les redondances de données","Dénormaliser les tables uniquement pour des lectures à haute performance","Utiliser UUID uniquement lorsque l''unicité globale est requise","Éviter la dénormalisation prématurée pour maintenir l''intégrité des données"],"de":["Primärschlüssel mit BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY definieren","Tabellen bis zur 3NF normalisieren, um Datenredundanz zu eliminieren","Tabellen nur für Hochleistungs-Lesevorgänge denormalisieren","UUID nur verwenden, wenn globale Eindeutigkeit erforderlich ist","Vorzeitige Denormalisierung vermeiden, um die Datenintegrität zu erhalten"],"pt":["Definição de PRIMARY KEY para referência de tabelas","Normalização para eliminar redundâncias de dados","Denormalização para melhorar o desempenho da leitura","Uso de BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY para IDs únicos","Uso de UUID para garantir a unicidade global"],"ru":["Определение PRIMARY KEY для ссылки на таблицы","Нормализация для исключения избыточности данных","Денормализация для улучшения производительности чтения","Использование BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY для уникальных идентификаторов","Использование UUID для обеспечения глобальной уникальности"],"ar":["تحديد PRIMARY KEY لمرجع الجداول","التطبيع لاستبعاد التكرار في البيانات","التنظيم لتحسين أداء القراءة","استخدام BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY للمعرفات الفريدة","استخدام UUID لضمان الفريدية العالمية"]},"keywords":{"en":["how to use postgresql-table-design","postgresql-table-design best practices","postgresql-table-design vs mysql","postgresql-table-design setup guide","postgresql-table-design install","postgresql-table-design tutorial","what is postgresql-table-design","postgresql-table-design alternative","postgresql-table-design optimization"],"zh":["PostgreSQL 表设计","PRIMARY KEY","Normalize","Denormalize","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","UUID","PostgreSQL 优化","数据库设计"],"ja":["PostgreSQL テーブル設計","PRIMARY KEY","Normalize","Denormalize","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","UUID","PostgreSQL 最適化","データベース設計"],"ko":["PostgreSQL 테이블 설계","PRIMARY KEY","Normalize","Denormalize","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","UUID","PostgreSQL 최적화","데이터베이스 설계"],"es":["diseño de tablas postgresql","normalización de tablas","denormalización de tablas","claves primarias en postgresql","uuid en postgresql","bigint generated always as identity","mejores prácticas para diseñar tablas","configuración de tablas en postgresql","herramientas de diseño de tablas"],"fr":["conception de tables postgresql","normalisation de tables","dénormalisation de tables","clés primaires dans postgresql","uuid dans postgresql","bigint generated always as identity","meilleures pratiques pour concevoir des tables","configuration de tables dans postgresql","outils de conception de tables"],"de":["tabellendesign in postgresql","normalisierung von tabellen","denormalisierung von tabellen","primärschlüssel in postgresql","uuid in postgresql","bigint generated always as identity","best practices für tabellendesign","konfiguration von tabellen in postgresql","tools für tabellendesign"],"pt":["postgresql table design","normalização de dados","denormalização de dados","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","UUID no postgresql","otimização de banco de dados","desenvolvimento de aplicativos"],"ru":["проектирование таблиц postgresql","нормализация данных","денормализация данных","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","UUID в postgresql","оптимизация базы данных","разработка приложений"],"ar":["تصميم الجداول في postgresql","تطبيع البيانات","تنظيم البيانات","BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY","UUID في postgresql","تحسين أداء قاعدة البيانات","تطوير التطبيقات"]}},"owner":"ollieb89","repo":"ml_challenges","repoPath":"ollieb89/ml_challenges","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-08T01:57:15.521Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"postgresql-table-design","description":"Design a PostgreSQL-specific schema. Covers best-practices, data types, indexing, constraints, performance patterns, and advanced features","bodyPreview":"# PostgreSQL Table Design \n\n## Core Rules\n\n- Define a **PRIMARY KEY** for reference tables (users, orders, etc.). Not always needed for time-series/event/log data. When used, prefer `BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY`; use `UUID` only when global uniqueness/opacity is needed.\n- **Normalize first (to 3NF)** to eliminate data redundancy and update anomalies; denormalize **only** for measured, high-ROI reads where join performance is proven problematic. Premature denormalization creates maintenan","body":"# PostgreSQL Table Design \n\n## Core Rules\n\n- Define a **PRIMARY KEY** for reference tables (users, orders, etc.). Not always needed for time-series/event/log data. When used, prefer `BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY`; use `UUID` only when global uniqueness/opacity is needed.\n- **Normalize first (to 3NF)** to eliminate data redundancy and update anomalies; denormalize **only** for measured, high-ROI reads where join performance is proven problematic. Premature denormalization creates maintenance burden.\n- Add **NOT NULL** everywhere it’s semantically required; use **DEFAULT**s for common values.\n- Create **indexes for access paths you actually query**: PK/unique (auto), **FK columns (manual!)**, frequent filters/sorts, and join keys.\n- Prefer **TIMESTAMPTZ** for event time; **NUMERIC** for money; **TEXT** for strings; **BIGINT** for integer values, **DOUBLE PRECISION** for floats (or `NUMERIC` for exact decimal arithmetic).\n\n## PostgreSQL “Gotchas”\n\n- **Identifiers**: unquoted → lowercased. Avoid quoted/mixed-case names. Convention: use `snake_case` for table/column names.\n- **Unique + NULLs**: UNIQUE allows multiple NULLs. Use `UNIQUE (...) NULLS NOT DISTINCT` (PG15+) to restrict to one NULL.\n- **FK indexes**: PostgreSQL **does not** auto-index FK columns. Add them.\n- **No silent coercions**: length/precision overflows error out (no truncation). Example: inserting 999 into `NUMERIC(2,0)` fails with error, unlike some databases that silently truncate or round.\n- **Sequences/identity have gaps** (normal; don''t \"fix\"). Rollbacks, crashes, and concurrent transactions create gaps in ID sequences (1, 2, 5, 6...). This is expected behavior—don''t try to make IDs consecutive.\n- **Heap storage**: no clustered PK by default (unlike SQL Server/MySQL InnoDB); `CLUSTER` is one-off reorganization, not maintained on subsequent inserts. Row order on disk is insertion order unless explicitly clustered.\n- **MVCC**: updates/deletes leave dead tuples; vacuum handles them—design to avoid hot wide-row churn.\n\n## Data Types\n\n- **IDs**: `BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY` preferred (`GENERATED BY DEFAULT` also fine); `UUID` when merging/federating/used in a distributed system or for opaque IDs. Generate with `uuidv7()` (preferred if using PG18+) or `gen_random_uuid()` (if using an older PG version).\n- **Integers**: prefer `BIGINT` unless storage space is critical; `INTEGER` for smaller ranges; avoid `SMALLINT` unless constrained.\n- **Floats**: prefer `DOUBLE PRECISION` over `REAL` unless storage space is critical. Use `NUMERIC` for exact decimal arithmetic.\n- **Strings**: prefer `TEXT`; if length limits needed, use `CHECK (LENGTH(col) <= n)` instead of `VARCHAR(n)`; avoid `CHAR(n)`. Use `BYTEA` for binary data. Large strings/binary (>2KB default threshold) automatically stored in TOAST with compression. TOAST storage: `PLAIN` (no TOAST), `EXTENDED` (compress + out-of-line), `EXTERNAL` (out-of-line, no compress), `MAIN` (compress, keep in-line if possible). Default `EXTENDED` usually optimal. Control with `ALTER TABLE tbl ALTER COLUMN col SET STORAGE strategy` and `ALTER TABLE tbl SET (toast_tuple_target = 4096)` for threshold. Case-insensitive: for locale/accent handling use non-deterministic collations; for plain ASCII use expression indexes on `LOWER(col)` (preferred unless column needs case-insensitive PK/FK/UNIQUE) or `CITEXT`.\n- **Money**: `NUMERIC(p,s)` (never float).\n- **Time**: `TIMESTAMPTZ` for timestamps; `DATE` for date-only; `INTERVAL` for durations. Avoid `TIMESTAMP` (without timezone). Use `now()` for transaction start time, `clock_timestamp()` for current wall-clock time.\n- **Booleans**: `BOOLEAN` with `NOT NULL` constraint unless tri-state values are required.\n- **Enums**: `CREATE TYPE ... AS ENUM` for small, stable sets (e.g. US states, days of week). For business-logic-driven and evolving values (e.g. order statuses) → use TEXT (or INT) + CHECK or lookup table.\n- **Arrays**: `TEXT[]`, `INTEGER[]`, etc. Use for ordered lists where you query elements. Index with **GIN** for containment (`@>`, `<@`) and overlap (`&&`) queries. Access: `arr[1]` (1-indexed), `arr[1:3]` (slicing). Good for tags, categories; avoid for relations—use junction tables instead. Literal syntax: `''{val1,val2}''` or `ARRAY[val1,val2]`.\n- **Range types**: `daterange`, `numrange`, `tstzrange` for intervals. Support overlap (`&&`), containment (`@>`), operators. Index with **GiST**. Good for scheduling, versioning, numeric ranges. Pick a bounds scheme and use it consistently; prefer `[)` (inclusive/exclusive) by default.\n- **Network types**: `INET` for IP addresses, `CIDR` for network ranges, `MACADDR` for MAC addresses. Support network operators (`<<`, `>>`, `&&`).\n- **Geometric types**: `POINT`, `LINE`, `POLYGON`, `CIRCLE` for 2D spatial data. Index with **GiST**. Consider **PostGIS** for advanced spatial features.\n- **Text search**: `TSVECTOR` for full-text search documents, `TSQUERY` for search queries. Index `tsvector` with **GIN**. Always specify language: `to_tsvector(''english'', col)` and `to_tsquery(''english'', ''query'')`. Never use single-argument versions. This applies to both index expressions and queries.\n- **Domain types**: `CREATE DOMAIN email AS TEXT CHECK (VALUE ~ ''^[^@]+@[^@]+$'')` for reusable custom types with validation. Enforces constraints across tables.\n- **Composite types**: `CREATE TYPE address AS (street TEXT, city TEXT, zip TEXT)` for structured data within columns. Access with `(col).field` syntax.\n- **JSONB**: preferred over JSON; index with **GIN**. Use only for optional/semi-structured attrs. ONLY use JSON if the original ordering of the contents MUST be preserved.\n- **Vector types**: `vector` type by `pgvector` for vector similarity search for embeddings.\n\n\n### Do not use the following data types\n- DO NOT use `timestamp` (without time zone); DO use `timestamptz` instead.\n- DO NOT use `char(n)` or `varchar(n)`; DO use `text` instead.\n- DO NOT use `money` type; DO use `numeric` instead.\n- DO NOT use `timetz` type; DO use `timestamptz` instead.\n- DO NOT use `timestamptz(0)` or any other precision specification; DO use `timestamptz` instead\n- DO NOT use `serial` type; DO use `generated always as identity` instead.\n\n\n## Table Types\n\n- **Regular**: default; fully durable, logged.\n- **TEMPORARY**: session-scoped, auto-dropped, not logged. Faster for scratch work.\n- **UNLOGGED**: persistent but not crash-safe. Faster writes; good for caches/staging.\n\n## Row-Level Security\n\nEnable with `ALTER TABLE tbl ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY`. Create policies: `CREATE POLICY user_access ON orders FOR SELECT TO app_users USING (user_id = current_user_id())`. Built-in user-based access control at the row level.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- **PK**: implicit UNIQUE + NOT NULL; creates a B-tree index.\n- **FK**: specify `ON DELETE/UPDATE` action (`CASCADE`, `RESTRICT`, `SET NULL`, `SET DEFAULT`). Add explicit index on referencing column—speeds up joins and prevents locking issues on parent deletes/updates. Use `DEFERRABLE INITIALLY DEFERRED` for circular FK dependencies checked at transaction end.\n- **UNIQUE**: creates a B-tree index; allows multiple NULLs unless `NULLS NOT DISTINCT` (PG15+). Standard behavior: `(1, NULL)` and `(1, NULL)` are allowed. With `NULLS NOT DISTINCT`: only one `(1, NULL)` allowed. Prefer `NULLS NOT DISTINCT` unless you specifically need duplicate NULLs.\n- **CHECK**: row-local constraints; NULL values pass the check (three-valued logic). Example: `CHECK (price > 0)` allows NULL prices. Combine with `NOT NULL` to enforce: `price NUMERIC NOT NULL CHECK (price > 0)`.\n- **EXCLUDE**: prevents overlapping values using operators. `EXCLUDE USING gist (room_id WITH =, booking_period WITH &&)` prevents double-booking rooms. Requires appropriate index type (often GiST).\n\n## Indexing\n\n- **B-tree**: default for equality/range queries (`=`, `<`, `>`, `BETWEEN`, `ORDER BY`)\n- **Composite**: order matters—index used if equality on leftmost prefix (`WHERE a = ? AND b > ?` uses index on `(a,b)`, but `WHERE b = ?` does not). Put most selective/frequently filtered columns first.\n- **Covering**: `CREATE INDEX ON tbl (id) INCLUDE (name, email)` - includes non-key columns for index-only scans without visiting table.\n- **Partial**: for hot subsets (`WHERE status = ''active''` → `CREATE INDEX ON tbl (user_id) WHERE status = ''active''`). Any query with `status = ''active''` can use this index.\n- **Expression**: for computed search keys (`CREATE INDEX ON tbl (LOWER(email))`). Expression must match exactly in WHERE clause: `WHERE LOWER(email) = ''user@example.com''`.\n- **GIN**: JSONB containment/existence, arrays (`@>`, `?`), full-text search (`@@`)\n- **GiST**: ranges, geometry, exclusion constraints\n- **BRIN**: very large, naturally ordered data (time-series)—minimal storage overhead. Effective when row order on disk correlates with indexed column (insertion order or after `CLUSTER`).\n\n## Partitioning\n\n- Use for very large tables (>100M rows) where queries consistently filter on partition key (often time/date).\n- Alternate use: use for tables where data maintenance tasks dictates e.g. data pruned or bulk replaced periodically\n- **RANGE**: common for time-series (`PARTITION BY RANGE (created_at)`). Create partitions: `CREATE TABLE logs_2024_01 PARTITION OF logs FOR VALUES FROM (''2024-01-01'') TO (''2024-02-01'')`. **TimescaleDB** automates time-based or ID-based partitioning with retention policies and compression.\n- **LIST**: for discrete values (`PARTITION BY LIST (region)`). Example: `FOR VALUES IN (''us-east'', ''us-west'')`.\n- **HASH**: for even distribution when no natural key (`PARTITION BY HASH (user_id)`). Creates N partitions with modulus.\n- **Constraint exclusion**: requires `CHECK` constraints on partitions for query planner to prune. Auto-created for declarative partitioning (PG10+).\n- Prefer declarative partitioning or hypertables. Do NOT use table inheritance.\n- **Limitations**: no global UNIQUE constraints—include partition key in PK/UNIQUE. FKs from partitioned tables not supported; use triggers.\n\n## Special Considerations\n\n### Update-Heavy Tables\n\n- **Separate hot/cold columns**—put frequently updated columns in separate table to minimize bloat.\n- **Use `fillfactor=90`** to leave space for HOT updates that avoid index maintenance.\n- **Avoid updating indexed columns**—prevents beneficial HOT updates.\n- **Partition by update patterns**—separate frequently updated rows in a different partition from stable data.\n\n### Insert-Heavy Workloads\n\n- **Minimize indexes**—only create what you query; every index slows inserts.\n- **Use `COPY` or multi-row `INSERT`** instead of single-row inserts.\n- **UNLOGGED tables** for rebuildable staging data—much faster writes.\n- **Defer index creation** for bulk loads—>drop index, load data, recreate indexes.\n- **Partition by time/hash** to distribute load. **TimescaleDB** automates partitioning and compression of insert-heavy data.\n- **Use a natural key for primary key** such as a (timestamp, device_id) if enforcing global uniqueness is important many insert-heavy tables don''t need a primary key at all.\n- If you do need a surrogate key, **Prefer `BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY` over `UUID`**.\n\n### Upsert-Friendly Design\n\n- **Requires UNIQUE index** on conflict target columns—`ON CONFLICT (col1, col2)` needs exact matching unique index (partial indexes don''t work).\n- **Use `EXCLUDED.column`** to reference would-be-inserted values; only update columns that actually changed to reduce write overhead.\n- **`DO NOTHING` faster** than `DO UPDATE` when no actual update needed.\n\n### Safe Schema Evolution\n\n- **Transactional DDL**: most DDL operations can run in transactions and be rolled back—`BEGIN; ALTER TABLE...; ROLLBACK;` for safe testing.\n- **Concurrent index creation**: `CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY` avoids blocking writes but can''t run in transactions.\n- **Volatile defaults cause rewrites**: adding `NOT NULL` columns with volatile defaults (e.g., `now()`, `gen_random_uuid()`) rewrites entire table. Non-volatile defaults are fast.\n- **Drop constraints before columns**: `ALTER TABLE DROP CONSTRAINT` then `DROP COLUMN` to avoid dependency issues.\n- **Function signature changes**: `CREATE OR REPLACE` with different arguments creates overloads, not replacements. DROP old version if no overload desired.\n\n## Generated Columns\n\n- `... GENERATED ALWAYS AS (<expr>) STORED` for computed, indexable fields. PG18+ adds `VIRTUAL` columns (computed on read, not stored).\n\n## Extensions\n\n- **`pgcrypto`**: `crypt()` for password hashing.\n- **`uuid-ossp`**: alternative UUID functions; prefer `pgcrypto` for new projects.\n- **`pg_trgm`**: fuzzy text search with `%` operator, `similarity()` function. Index with GIN for `LIKE ''%pattern%''` acceleration.\n- **`citext`**: case-insensitive text type. Prefer expression indexes on `LOWER(col)` unless you need case-insensitive constraints.\n- **`btree_gin`/`btree_gist`**: enable mixed-type indexes (e.g., GIN index on both JSONB and text columns).\n- **`hstore`**: key-value pairs; mostly superseded by JSONB but useful for simple string mappings.\n- **`timescaledb`**: essential for time-series—automated partitioning, retention, compression, continuous aggregates.\n- **`postgis`**: comprehensive geospatial support beyond basic geometric types—essential for location-based applications.\n- **`pgvector`**: vector similarity search for embeddings.\n- **`pgaudit`**: audit logging for all database activity.\n\n## JSONB Guidance\n\n- Prefer `JSONB` with **GIN** index.\n- Default: `CREATE INDEX ON tbl USING GIN (jsonb_col);` → accelerates:\n  - **Containment** `jsonb_col @> ''{\"k\":\"v\"}''`\n  - **Key existence** `jsonb_col ? ''k''`, **any/all keys** `?\\|`, `?&`\n  - **Path containment** on nested docs\n  - **Disjunction** `jsonb_col @> ANY(ARRAY[''{\"status\":\"active\"}'', ''{\"status\":\"pending\"}''])`\n- Heavy `@>` workloads: consider opclass `jsonb_path_ops` for smaller/faster containment-only indexes:\n  - `CREATE INDEX ON tbl USING GIN (jsonb_col jsonb_path_ops);`\n  - **Trade-off**: loses support for key existence (`?`, `?|`, `?&`) queries—only supports containment (`@>`)\n- Equality/range on a specific scalar field: extract and index with B-tree (generated column or expression):\n  - `ALTER TABLE tbl ADD COLUMN price INT GENERATED ALWAYS AS ((jsonb_col->>''price'')::INT) STORED;`\n  - `CREATE INDEX ON tbl (price);`\n  - Prefer queries like `WHERE price BETWEEN 100 AND 500` (uses B-tree) over `WHERE (jsonb_col->>''price'')::INT BETWEEN 100 AND 500` without index.\n- Arrays inside JSONB: use GIN + `@>` for containment (e.g., tags). Consider `jsonb_path_ops` if only doing containment.\n- Keep core relations in tables; use JSONB for optional/variable attributes.\n- Use constraints to limit allowed JSONB values in a column e.g. `config JSONB NOT NULL CHECK(jsonb_typeof(config) = ''object'')`\n\n\n## Examples\n\n### Users\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE users (\n  user_id BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY,\n  email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  name TEXT NOT NULL,\n  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()\n);\nCREATE UNIQUE INDEX ON users (LOWER(email));\nCREATE INDEX ON users (created_at);\n```\n\n### Orders\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE orders (\n  order_id BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY,\n  user_id BIGINT NOT NULL REFERENCES users(user_id),\n  status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT ''PENDING'' CHECK (status IN (''PENDING'',''PAID'',''CANCELED'')),\n  total NUMERIC(10,2) NOT NULL CHECK (total > 0),\n  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()\n);\nCREATE INDEX ON orders (user_id);\nCREATE INDEX ON orders (created_at);\n```\n\n### JSONB\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE profiles (\n  user_id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY REFERENCES users(user_id),\n  attrs JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT ''{}'',\n  theme TEXT GENERATED ALWAYS AS (attrs->>''theme'') STORED\n);\nCREATE INDEX profiles_attrs_gin ON profiles USING GIN (attrs);\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-08T02:10:43.608Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Database Administration Agents needing efficient PostgreSQL table design and normalization expertise.","zh":"非常适合需要高效PostgreSQL表设计和规范化专业知识的数据库管理代理。","ja":"PostgreSQLのテーブル設計と正規化の専門知識が必要なデータベース管理エージェントに最適です。","ko":"효율적인 PostgreSQL 테이블 설계 및 정규화 전문 지식이 필요한 데이터베이스 관리 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de administración de bases de datos que necesitan un diseño eficiente de tablas de PostgreSQL y experiencia en normalización.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''administration de bases de données nécessitant une conception de table PostgreSQL efficace et une expertise en normalisation.","de":"Perfekt für Datenbank-Administations-Agents, die effizientes PostgreSQL-Tabellendesign und Normalisierungsexpertise benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Administração de Banco de Dados que necessitam de design eficiente de tabelas PostgreSQL e especialização em normalização.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов администрирования баз данных, которым требуется эффективный дизайн таблиц PostgreSQL и экспертиза в области нормализации.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء إدارة قواعد البيانات الذين يحتاجون إلى تصميم جداول PostgreSQL فعال وخبرة في التطبيع."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to define optimal PRIMARY KEYs using BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY, normalize data to 3NF, and strategically denormalize for high-ROI reads, leveraging UUID for global uniqueness when necessary.","zh":"赋予代理定义使用BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY的最佳主键，规范化数据到3NF，并在必要时利用UUID进行战略性反规范化以实现高投资回报率的读取，","ja":"エージェントがBIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITYを使用した最適な主キーを定義し、データを3NFに正規化し、必要に応じてUUIDを使用して戦略的に反正規化して、高投資回収率の読み取りを実現することを可能にします。","ko":"에이전트가 BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY를 사용하여 최적의 기본 키를 정의하고 데이터를 3NF로 정규화하며 필요에 따라 UUID를 사용하여 전략적으로 비정규화하여 높은 투자수익률의 읽기를 달성할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a definir claves primarias óptimas utilizando BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY, normalizar datos a 3NF y denormalizar estratégicamente para lecturas de alto ROI, aprovechando UUID para la unicidad global cuando sea necesario.","fr":"Permet aux agents de définir des clés primaires optimales en utilisant BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY, normaliser les données à 3NF et dénormaliser stratégiquement pour des lectures à haut ROI, en exploitant UUID pour l''unicité globale lorsque nécessaire.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, optimale PRIMARY KEYs unter Verwendung von BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY zu definieren, Daten zu 3NF zu normalisieren und strategisch zu denormalisieren, um einen hohen ROI bei Lesevorgängen zu erzielen, wobei UUID für globale Eindeutigkeit genutzt wird, wenn erforderlich.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a definir chaves primárias ótimas usando BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY, normalizar dados para 3NF e desnormalizar estrategicamente para leituras de alto ROI, utilizando UUID para unicidade global quando necessário.","ru":"Позволяет агентам определять оптимальные первичные ключи с помощью BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY, нормализовать данные до 3NF и стратегически денормализовать для чтений с высокой отдачей инвестиций, используя UUID для глобальной уникальности при необходимости.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تعريف المفاتيح الرئيسية المثالية باستخدام BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY، وتنسيق البيانات إلى 3NF، وتنزيل التطبيع بشكل استراتيجي لقراءات عالية العائد على الاستثمار، واستخدام UUID لضمان الفروق العالمية عند الحاجة."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing reference tables with efficient primary keys","Normalizing data to eliminate redundancy and update anomalies","Denormalizing for measured, high-ROI reads to improve join performance"],"zh":["使用高效主键设计引用表","规范化数据以消除冗余和更新异常","为了提高连接性能而进行测量、高投资回报率的读取的反规范化"],"ja":["効率的な主キーを使用した参照テーブルの設計","冗長性と更新の異常を排除するためのデータの正規化","ジョインのパフォーマンスを向上させるための計測済み、高投資回収率の読み取りの反正規化"],"ko":["효율적인 기본 키를 사용한 참조 테이블 설계","중복과 업데이트 이상을 제거하기 위한 데이터 정규화","조인 성능을 개선하기 위한 측정된 높은 투자수익률의 읽기 위한 비정규화"],"es":["Diseñar tablas de referencia con claves primarias eficientes","Normalizar datos para eliminar la redundancia y las anomalías de actualización","Denormalizar para lecturas medibles con alto ROI y mejorar el rendimiento de unión"],"fr":["Concevoir des tables de référence avec des clés primaires efficaces","Normaliser les données pour éliminer la redondance et les anomalies de mise à jour","Dénormaliser pour des lectures mesurées à haut ROI et améliorer les performances de jointure"],"de":["Entwerfen von Referenztabelle mit effizienten Primärschlüsseln","Normalisieren von Daten, um Redundanz und Aktualisierungsanomalien zu beseitigen","Denormalisieren für gemessene, hochrentable Lesevorgänge, um die Leistung von Joins zu verbessern"],"pt":["Projetar tabelas de referência com chaves primárias eficientes","Normalizar dados para eliminar a redundância e anomalias de atualização","Desnormalizar para leituras medidas de alto ROI para melhorar o desempenho de junção"],"ru":["Проектирование таблиц справочников с эффективными первичными ключами","Нормализация данных для устранения избыточности и аномалий обновления","Денормализация для измеренных чтений с высокой отдачей инвестиций для улучшения производительности соединений"],"ar":["تصميم جداول المراجع ذات المفاتيح الرئيسية الفعالة","تنسيق البيانات للتخلص من التكرار واضطرابات التحديث","التنزيل التطبيعي لقراءات المقاسة ذات العائد العالي على الاستثمار لتحسين أداء الانضمام"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of database design principles","PostgreSQL-specific syntax and best practices","May require additional consideration for time-series, event, or log data"],"zh":["需要了解数据库设计原则","PostgreSQL特有的语法和最佳实践","可能需要对时间序列、事件或日志数据进行额外的考虑"],"ja":["データベース設計の原則の理解が必要","PostgreSQL特有の構文とベストプラクティス","時系列、イベント、またはログデータには追加の考慮が必要になる場合がある"],"ko":["데이터베이스 설계 원칙에 대한 이해가 필요","PostgreSQL 고유의 구문과 모범 사례","시간 순서, 이벤트 또는 로그 데이터의 경우 추가적인 고려가 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de los principios de diseño de bases de datos","Sintaxis y prácticas recomendadas específicas de PostgreSQL","Puede requerir consideraciones adicionales para datos de series temporales, eventos o registros"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des principes de conception de bases de données","Syntaxe et bonnes pratiques spécifiques à PostgreSQL","Peut nécessiter des considérations supplémentaires pour les données de série temporelle, d''événement ou de journal"],"de":["Benötigt Verständnis der Datenbank-Design-Prinzipien","PostgreSQL-spezifische Syntax und Best Practices","Kann zusätzliche Überlegungen für Zeitreihen-, Ereignis- oder Log-Daten erfordern"],"pt":["Exige compreensão dos princípios de design de banco de dados","Sintaxe e práticas recomendadas específicas do PostgreSQL","Pode exigir consideração adicional para dados de série temporal, eventos ou logs"],"ru":["Требует понимания принципов проектирования баз данных","Специфическая синтаксис и рекомендации для PostgreSQL","Может потребовать дополнительного учета для данных временных рядов, событий или журналов"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم مبادئ تصميم قواعد البيانات","yntax وافضل الممارسات الخاصة ببرنامج PostgreSQL","قد يتطلب考虑ًا إضافيًا للبيانات الزمنية أو الأحداث أو السجلات"]},"version":4},"contentHash":"05006a2c3f1fdc68dd308e8a7ad7daffd7e8f7b910643d241e31e4484110b107","qualityScore":54}');
DELETE FROM skills_fts WHERE id = 'ollieb89/ml_challenges/postgresql-table-design';
INSERT INTO skills_fts (id, name, owner, repo, category, search_text) VALUES ('ollieb89/ml_challenges/postgresql-table-design', 'postgresql-table-design', 'ollieb89', 'ml_challenges', 'community', 'postgresql-table-design ollieb89 ml_challenges community The PostgreSQL table design skill provides expert guidance on designing efficient database tables, benefiting developers and database administrators. It covers core rules, such as defining primary keys and normalizing data. PostgreSQL 表设计需要遵循特定的规则和最佳实践，包括定义主键和 Normalize。 PostgreSQL テーブル設計では、PRIMARY KEY の定義と Normalize が重要です。 PostgreSQL 테이블 설계는 PRIMARY KEY와 Normalize를 정의하는 것이 중요합니다. El diseño de tablas en PostgreSQL es crucial para una base de datos eficiente. Aprende a normalizar y denormalizar tus tablas La conception de tables dans PostgreSQL est essentielle pour une base de données efficace. Découvrez comment normaliser et dénormaliser vos tables Das Tabellendesign in PostgreSQL ist entscheidend für eine effiziente Datenbank. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie Ihre Tabellen normalisieren und denormalisieren Desenvolva habilidades em design de tabelas PostgreSQL, incluindo normalização e denormalização para melhorar o desempenho da aplicação Разработайте навыки в проектировании таблиц PostgreSQL, включая нормализацию и денормализацию для улучшения производительности приложения طور مهاراتك في تصميم الجداول في PostgreSQL، بما في ذلك التطبيع والتنظيم لتحسين أداء التطبيق how to use postgresql-table-design postgresql-table-design best practices postgresql-table-design vs mysql postgresql-table-design setup guide postgresql-table-design install postgresql-table-design tutorial what is postgresql-table-design postgresql-table-design alternative postgresql-table-design optimization PostgreSQL 表设计 PRIMARY KEY Normalize Denormalize BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY UUID PostgreSQL 优化 数据库设计 Defines primary keys using BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY Normalizes data to 3NF to eliminate redundancy and update anomalies Denormalizes data for high-ROI reads with proven join performance issues Uses UUID for global uniqueness and opacity when necessary Optimizes table design for time-series, event, and log data postgresql-table-design is a set of guidelines and best practices for creating efficient and scalable database tables in PostgreSQL, focusing on primary keys, normalization, and denormalization.');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('leboncoin/spark-web/create-component', 'community', 'leboncoin', 'spark-web', 'leboncoin/spark-web', 'create-component', 0, 0, 54, '2026-03-08T01:57:15.506Z', '2026-03-08T02:11:22.544Z', '880d935955e4e65fd88a59909f6afd69f9c1ee38b3226e12e95af31dc88bda05', '{"id":"leboncoin/spark-web/create-component","name":"create-component","description":{"en":"The create-component skill generates new Spark UI components for React applications, following the project''s standards and file structure. This skill benefits React developers looking to create modular and accessible UI components.","zh":"创建组件是用于创建简单、模块化和可访问的 React UI 组件的技术，提供最佳实践和设置指南","ja":"コンポーネントの作成は、React アプリケーションの UI コンポーネントを作成するための技術で、ベストプラクティスと設定ガイドを提供","ko":"컴포넌트 생성은 리액트 애플리케이션의 UI 컴포넌트를 생성하는 기술로, 튜토리얼과 설정 가이드를 제공","es":"Crea componentes de UI simples, modulares y accesibles para tus aplicaciones React. Determina la ubicación del componente y crea la estructura de archivos.","fr":"Créez des composants UI simples, modulaires et accessibles pour vos applications React. Déterminez l''emplacement du composant et créez la structure de fichiers.","de":"Erstellen Sie einfache, modulare und zugängliche UI-Komponenten für Ihre React-Anwendungen. Bestimmen Sie den Speicherort des Komponenten und erstellen Sie die Dateistruktur.","pt":"O Create-Component é uma ferramenta para criar componentes UI modulares e acessíveis para aplicações React","ru":"ИИ Агент Create-Component позволяет создавать модульные и доступные компоненты UI для приложений React","ar":"Create-Component هو أداة لإنشاء مكونات واجهة المستخدم القابلة للتشغيل والoppable للتفاعلات React"},"seo":{"title":{"en":"create-component: Setup Guide for React Applications | AI...","zh":"创建组件 Setup Guide - 简单的 React 应用 UI 组件","ja":"コンポーネントの作成 Best Practices - React アプリケーションの UI コンポーネント","ko":"컴포넌트 생성 Tutorial - 리액트 애플리케이션의 UI 컴포넌트","es":"Crear Componentes de UI para React: Guía de Configuración","fr":"Créer des Composants UI pour React: Meilleures Pratiques","de":"Erstellen von UI-Komponenten für React: Einrichtungsanlei...","pt":"Guia de Configuração do Create-Component para React","ru":"ИИ Агент Create-Component: Руководство по Настройке для R...","ar":"دليل إعداد Create-Component للتفاعلات React"},"description":{"en":"Discover how to create modular UI components for React with our create-component skill. Learn how to get started and implement new components today!","zh":"使用 create-component 技术创建简单、模块化和可访问的 React UI 组件，了解最佳实践和设置指南","ja":"React アプリケーションの UI コンポーネントを作成するための create-component 技術の使い方とベストプラクティス","ko":"리액트 애플리케이션의 UI 컴포넌트를 생성하는 create-component 기술의 사용 방법과 튜토리얼","es":"Aprende a crear componentes de UI modulares y accesibles para tus aplicaciones React con nuestra guía paso a paso de herramientas de inteligencia artificial","fr":"Découvrez comment créer des composants UI simples et modulaires pour vos applications React avec notre guide étape par étape d''outils d''intelligence artifici...","de":"Erfahren Sie, wie Sie modulare und zugängliche UI-Komponenten für Ihre React-Anwendungen mit unserer schrittweisen Anleitung zu KI-Tools erstellen","pt":"Aprenda a criar componentes UI modulares e acessíveis para suas aplicações React com o Create-Component","ru":"Создавайте модульные и доступные компоненты UI для приложений React с помощью ИИ Агента Create-Component","ar":"ابني مكونات واجهة المستخدم القابلة للتشغيل والoppable مع Create-Component للتفاعلات React"},"definition":{"en":"create-component is a skill that creates new Spark UI components for React applications, following a standardized file structure and project guidelines.","zh":"create-component 是一种用于创建 React UI 组件的技术，提供简单、模块化和可访问的组件","ja":"コンポーネントの作成は、React UI コンポーネントを作成するための技術で、シンプル、モジュラー、可 доступ性の高いコンポーネントを提供","ko":"컴포넌트 생성은 리액트 UI 컴포넌트를 생성하는 기술로, 단순한, 모듈화된, 접근 가능한 컴포넌트를 제공","es":"El create-component es una herramienta de inteligencia artificial que permite a los desarrolladores crear componentes de UI personalizados para aplicaciones React","fr":"Le create-component est un outil d''intelligence artificielle qui permet aux développeurs de créer des composants UI personnalisés pour les applications React","de":"Der create-component ist ein KI-Tool, das es Entwicklern ermöglicht, benutzerdefinierte UI-Komponenten für React-Anwendungen zu erstellen","pt":"O Create-Component é uma ferramenta para criar componentes UI modulares","ru":"ИИ Агент Create-Component - это инструмент для создания модульных компонентов UI","ar":"Create-Component هو أداة لإنشاء مكونات واجهة المستخدم القابلة للتشغيل"},"features":{"en":["Creates new Spark UI components in the packages/components/src/<component-name>/ directory","Follows the project''s standards and file structure for consistency","Determines component location based on the project''s guidelines","Creates a file structure with a ComponentName.tsx file for each new component","Supports React applications with modular and accessible UI components"],"zh":["使用 React 创建简单、模块化的 UI 组件","提供可访问的 UI 组件","遵循项目的标准和文件结构","支持 TypeScript","提供最佳实践和设置指南"],"ja":["React を使用してシンプルなモジュラーな UI コンポーネントを作成","アクセス可能な UI コンポーネントを提供","プロジェクトの標準とファイル構造に従う","TypeScript をサポート","ベストプラクティスと設定ガイドを提供"],"ko":["리액트를 사용하여 단순한 모듈화된 UI 컴포넌트를 생성","접근 가능한 UI 컴포넌트를 제공","프로젝트의 표준과 파일 구조를 따름","타입스크립트를 지원","튜토리얼과 설정 가이드를 제공"],"es":["Crea componentes de UI modulares y accesibles","Determina la ubicación del componente en `packages/components/src/<component-name>/`","Crea la estructura de archivos con `ComponentName.tsx`","Seguimiento de las normas y estructura de proyecto de Spark UI","Compatibilidad con aplicaciones React","Soporte para la implementación de componentes desde diseños"],"fr":["Créez des composants UI modulaires et accessibles","Déterminez l''emplacement du composant en `packages/components/src/<component-name>/`","Créez la structure de fichiers avec `ComponentName.tsx`","Suivi des normes et de la structure de projet de Spark UI","Compatibilité avec les applications React","Prise en charge de la mise en œuvre de composants à partir de conceptions"],"de":["Erstellen Sie modulare und zugängliche UI-Komponenten","Bestimmen Sie den Speicherort des Komponenten in `packages/components/src/<component-name>/`","Erstellen Sie die Dateistruktur mit `ComponentName.tsx`","Einhaltung der Standards und Projektstruktur von Spark UI","Kompatibilität mit React-Anwendungen","Unterstützung für die Implementierung von Komponenten aus Designs"],"pt":["Criação de componentes UI modulares e acessíveis","Integração com o padrão de projeto React","Estrutura de arquivos personalizável","Suporte a TypeScript","Compatibilidade com React Applications"],"ru":["Создание модульных и доступных компонентов UI","Интеграция с стандартом проекта React","Настраиваемая структура файлов","Поддержка TypeScript","Совместимость с приложениями React"],"ar":["إنشاء مكونات واجهة المستخدم القابلة للتشغيل والoppable","التكامل مع معيار مشروع React","هيكل الملفات القابل للتعديل","دعم TypeScript","التوافق مع تطبيقات React"]},"keywords":{"en":["how to use create-component","create-component setup guide","create-component for React","create-component alternative","create-component vs other UI component tools","install create-component","what is create-component","create-component tutorial","create-component best practices"],"zh":["create-component","React UI 组件","简单组件","模块化组件","可访问组件","React 技术","AI エージェント","前端开发"],"ja":["コンポーネントの作成","React UI コンポーネント","シンプルなコンポーネント","モジュラーなコンポーネント","アクセス可能なコンポーネント","React 技術","AI エージェント","フロントエンド開発"],"ko":["컴포넌트 생성","리액트 UI 컴포넌트","단순한 컴포넌트","모듈화된 컴포넌트","접근 가능한 컴포넌트","리액트 기술","AI 에이전트","프론트엔드 개발"],"es":["create-component","herramientas de inteligencia artificial","componentes de UI para React","guias de configuración para React","mejores prácticas para componentes de UI","diseño de componentes UI","desarrollo de aplicaciones React","react js","ui components","ai tools"],"fr":["create-component","outils d''intelligence artificielle","composants UI pour React","guides de configuration pour React","meilleures pratiques pour les composants UI","conception de composants UI","développement d''applications React","react js","ui components","ai tools"],"de":["create-component","KI-Tools","UI-Komponenten für React","Einrichtungsanleitungen für React","Best Practices für UI-Komponenten","Entwurf von UI-Komponenten","Entwicklung von React-Anwendungen","react js","ui components","ai tools"],"pt":["Create-Component","React","Componentes UI","Modulares","Acessíveis","Guia de Configuração","Ferramentas de Desenvolvimento","Desenvolvimento de Aplicativos"],"ru":["ИИ Агент Create-Component","React","Компоненты UI","Модульные","Доступные","Руководство по Настройке","Инструменты разработки","Разработка приложений"],"ar":["Create-Component","React","مكونات واجهة المستخدم","القابلة للتشغيل","الoppable","دليل إعداد","أدوات التطوير","تطوير التطبيقات"]}},"owner":"leboncoin","repo":"spark-web","repoPath":"leboncoin/spark-web","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-08T01:57:15.506Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"create-component","description":"Create a new Spark UI component with complete file structure including component, styles, tests, stories, and documentation. Use when the user wants to create a new component or add a component to the design system.","bodyPreview":"# Create Component\n\nCreate a new Spark UI component following the project''s standards and file structure.\n\n## When to Use\n\n- User wants to create a new component\n- User mentions \"new component\", \"add component\", or \"create component\"\n- User is implementing a component from a design\n\n## Instructions\n\n1. **Determine component location**: Components go in `packages/components/src/<component-name>/`\n\n2. **Create the file structure**:\n   ```\n   component-name/\n   ├── ComponentName.tsx           # Mai","body":"# Create Component\n\nCreate a new Spark UI component following the project''s standards and file structure.\n\n## When to Use\n\n- User wants to create a new component\n- User mentions \"new component\", \"add component\", or \"create component\"\n- User is implementing a component from a design\n\n## Instructions\n\n1. **Determine component location**: Components go in `packages/components/src/<component-name>/`\n\n2. **Create the file structure**:\n   ```\n   component-name/\n   ├── ComponentName.tsx           # Main component\n   ├── ComponentName.styles.tsx    # Styling with CVA\n   ├── ComponentName.test.tsx      # Unit tests\n   ├── ComponentName.stories.tsx   # Storybook stories\n   ├── ComponentName.doc.mdx       # Documentation\n   ├── index.ts                    # Exports\n   └── variants/                   # Style variants (if applicable)\n   ```\n\n3. **Component Implementation**:\n   - Use TypeScript with strict typing\n   - Implement polymorphic behavior with `asChild` prop if needed\n   - Use CVA (Class Variance Authority) for styling variants\n   - Include `data-spark-component` attribute\n   - Ensure WCAG 2.1 AA compliance\n   - Use proper ARIA attributes\n\n4. **Styling**:\n   - Create `ComponentName.styles.tsx` with CVA\n   - Define variants (size, variant, etc.)\n   - Use TailwindCSS classes\n\n5. **Tests**:\n   - Create `ComponentName.test.tsx` with Vitest + React Testing Library\n   - Test rendering, props, variants, and accessibility\n   - Test user interactions\n\n6. **Stories**:\n   - Create `ComponentName.stories.tsx` following Storybook CSF format\n   - Use `Components/*` meta structure\n   - Create stories for: Default, Uncontrolled, Controlled, and other variants\n   - One story per prop/feature\n\n7. **Documentation**:\n   - Create `ComponentName.doc.mdx` with sections in this order:\n     - Title (H1)\n     - Meta (link to stories)\n     - Install\n     - Import\n     - Props table (using ArgTypes component)\n     - Usage (Default, Uncontrolled, Controlled, others alphabetically)\n     - Advanced Usage\n     - Accessibility\n\n8. **Exports**:\n   - Create `index.ts` with named exports\n   - Export component, types, and sub-components if compound\n\n9. **For Compound Components**:\n   - Use Object.assign pattern\n   - Set display names for all sub-components\n   - Document sub-components in ArgTypes\n\n10. **Verify**:\n    - Run `npm run lint` to check code quality\n    - Run `npm run typecheck` to verify types\n    - Run tests to ensure they pass\n    - Check Storybook renders correctly\n\n## Examples\n\nReference existing components in `packages/components/src/` for patterns:\n- Simple component: `badge/`, `button/`\n- Compound component: `card/`, `input/`, `accordion/`\n- Complex component: `combobox/`, `select/`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-08T02:11:22.544Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Frontend Agents specializing in React applications, seeking to generate modular and accessible UI components.","zh":"适用于专注于React应用的前端代理，旨在生成模块化和可访问的UI组件。","ja":"Reactアプリケーションを専門とするフロントエンドエージェントに適しています。モジュラーでアクセス可能なUIコンポーネントを生成することを目指しています。","ko":"React 애플리케이션을 전문으로 하는 프론트엔드 에이전트에게 적합합니다. 모듈화되고 접근 가능한 UI 컴포넌트를 생성하려고 합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes Frontend especializados en aplicaciones React, que buscan generar componentes de UI modulares y accesibles.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents Frontend spécialisés dans les applications React, qui cherchent à générer des composants d''interface utilisateur modulaires et accessibles.","de":"Ideal für Frontend-Agenten, die auf React-Anwendungen spezialisiert sind und modulare sowie zugängliche Benutzeroberflächenkomponenten generieren möchten.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Frontend especializados em aplicações React, que buscam gerar componentes de UI modulares e acessíveis.","ru":"Идеально для агентов Frontend, специализирующихся на приложениях React, стремящихся создавать модульные и доступные компоненты UI.","ar":"مثالي لعميل واجهة المستخدم الأمامية المتخصصة في تطبيقات React ، التي تهدف إلى إنشاء مكونات واجهة المستخدم القابلة للتحديث والمتوافقة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create new Spark UI components following project standards and file structure, utilizing React and TypeScript, and generating component files such as ComponentName.tsx.","zh":"赋予代理创建新Spark UI组件的能力，遵循项目标准和文件结构，利用React和TypeScript，并生成诸如ComponentName.tsx的组件文件。","ja":"エージェントがReactとTypeScriptを利用して、プロジェクトの標準とファイル構造に従った新しいSpark UIコンポーネントを作成する能力を提供します。コンポーネントファイル（たとえば、ComponentName.tsx）を生成します。","ko":"에이전트가 React와 TypeScript를 사용하여 프로젝트의 표준과 파일 구조에 따라 새로운 Spark UI 컴포넌트를 생성할 수 있도록 합니다. ComponentName.tsx와 같은 컴포넌트 파일을 생성합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear nuevos componentes de UI de Spark siguiendo los estándares del proyecto y la estructura de archivos, utilizando React y TypeScript, y generando archivos de componentes como ComponentName.tsx.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer de nouveaux composants d''interface utilisateur Spark en suivant les normes du projet et la structure de fichiers, en utilisant React et TypeScript, et en générant des fichiers de composants tels que ComponentName.tsx.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, neue Spark-Benutzeroberflächenkomponenten zu erstellen, die den Projektstandards und der Dateistruktur folgen, wobei React und TypeScript verwendet werden und Komponentendateien wie ComponentName.tsx generiert werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar novos componentes de UI do Spark, seguindo os padrões e a estrutura de arquivos do projeto, utilizando React e TypeScript, e gerando arquivos de componentes como ComponentName.tsx.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать новые компоненты UI Spark, следующими за стандартами и структурой файлов проекта, используя React и TypeScript, и генерируя файлы компонентов, такие как ComponentName.tsx.","ar":"يمكن للعميل إنشاء مكونات UI Spark الجديدة التي تتبع معايير ومخطط ملفات المشروع ، باستخدام React و TypeScript ، وإنشاء ملفات المكونات مثل ComponentName.tsx."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating new UI components for React applications","Creating modular components for improved code reusability","Implementing components from design specifications"],"zh":["为React应用程序生成新的UI组件","创建模块化的组件以提高代码的可重用性","根据设计规范实现组件"],"ja":["Reactアプリケーションの新しいUIコンポーネントを生成する","コードの再利用性を向上させるためにモジュラーなコンポーネントを作成する","デザイン仕様に基づいてコンポーネントを実装する"],"ko":["React 애플리케이션을 위한 새로운 UI 컴포넌트를 생성하는 것","코드의 재사용성을 높이기 위한 모듈화된 컴포넌트를 생성하는 것","디자인 사양에 따라 컴포넌트를 구현하는 것"],"es":["Generar nuevos componentes de UI para aplicaciones React","Crear componentes modulares para una mejor reutilización de código","Implementar componentes a partir de especificaciones de diseño"],"fr":["Générer de nouveaux composants d''interface utilisateur pour les applications React","Créer des composants modulaires pour améliorer la réutilisation du code","Mettre en œuvre des composants à partir de spécifications de conception"],"de":["Erstellen neuer Benutzeroberflächenkomponenten für React-Anwendungen","Erstellen moduler Komponenten zur Verbesserung der Code-Wiederverwendbarkeit","Implementieren von Komponenten aus Designspezifikationen"],"pt":["Geração de novos componentes de UI para aplicações React","Criação de componentes modulares para melhor reutilização de código","Implementação de componentes a partir de especificações de design"],"ru":["Генерация новых компонентов UI для приложений React","Создание модульных компонентов для улучшения повторного использования кода","Реализация компонентов на основе спецификаций дизайна"],"ar":["إنشاء مكونات UI جديدة لتطبيقات React","إنشاء مكونات قابلة للتحديث لتحسين إعادة استخدام الكود","تنفيذ المكونات من مواصفات التصميم"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of React and TypeScript","Specific to Spark UI components","Adherence to project''s standards and file structure necessary"],"zh":["需要了解React和TypeScript","仅限于Spark UI组件","需要遵守项目的标准和文件结构"],"ja":["ReactとTypeScriptの知識が必要","Spark UIコンポーネントに限定される","プロジェクトの標準とファイル構造に従う必要がある"],"ko":["React와 TypeScript에 대한 지식이 필요함","Spark UI 컴포넌트에 한정됨","프로젝트의 표준과 파일 구조를 따라야 함"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de React y TypeScript","Específico para componentes de UI de Spark","Necesario el cumplimiento de los estándares y la estructura de archivos del proyecto"],"fr":["Nécessite des connaissances en React et TypeScript","Spécifique aux composants d''interface utilisateur Spark","Le respect des normes et de la structure de fichiers du projet est nécessaire"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse von React und TypeScript","Spezifisch für Spark-Benutzeroberflächenkomponenten","Einhaltung der Projektstandards und der Dateistruktur ist erforderlich"],"pt":["Requer conhecimento de React e TypeScript","Específico para componentes de UI do Spark","Necessária aderência aos padrões e estrutura de arquivos do projeto"],"ru":["Требует знания React и TypeScript","Конкретно для компонентов UI Spark","Необходимо соблюдение стандартов и структуры файлов проекта"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة React و TypeScript","محدد لمكونات UI Spark","الامتثال لمعايير ومخطط ملفات المشروع ضروري"]},"version":4},"contentHash":"880d935955e4e65fd88a59909f6afd69f9c1ee38b3226e12e95af31dc88bda05","qualityScore":54}');
